Requirements:
- Generate a valid YAML playbook that passes ansible-lint.
- Follow the original task names and order exactly.
- Only fix linting issues reported; do not alter the functional intent or add/remove tasks.
- Output must consist solely of the corrected YAML playbook.

Inputs:
- Original generation prompt:
Below you will receive task descriptions from which you should generate an Ansible Playbook.

The generated playbook must be valid inside an Ansible Role under the tasks/ directory (e.g., tasks/main.yml).

Do not include hosts:, vars:, or any playbook-level headers. Only output valid task entries or blocks as expected in a role.

Task 1: Import and run tasks from assert.yml playbook.
Description Task 1: Import and run tasks from the assert.yml playbook on the localhost, running it only once, and delegating the task to the localhost.

Task 2: Install required packages for the service.
Description Task 2: Install the packages specified in the service_required_packages variable, ensuring they are present on the system.

Task 3: Configure systemd service for each item in the service_list.
Description Task 3: For each service in the service_list, configure the systemd service by copying the template "systemd.j2" to the destination "/etc/systemd/system/{{ item.name }}.service" with specific permissions, if the system uses systemd. After configuring, reload the daemon and notify the "Systemctl daemon-reload" handler.

Task 4: Configure sysvinit service for each item in the service_list.
Description Task 4: For each service in the service_list, configure the sysvinit service by copying the template "sysvinit.j2" to the destination "/etc/init.d/{{ item.name }}" with specific permissions, if the system uses sysvinit, upstart, or openrc. The "sysvinit" family of init systems handles service configuration in a different manner compared to systemd.

Task 5: Manage each service in the service_list.
Description Task 5: Manage the services listed in the service_list by enabling or disabling them according to their state. The state and enabled status are determined from the service_list's items. If a service's state is defined, or if its enabled status is defined, it will be managed accordingly.

Task 6: Flush handlers.
Description Task 6: Manually flush all handlers that have been notified during the execution of the playbook.


- Last generated (faulty) playbook:
---
- name: Import and run tasks from assert.yml playbook
  import_playbook: assert.yml
  delegate_to: localhost
  run_once: true

- name: Install required packages for the service
  package:
    name: "{{ item }}"
    state: present
  loop: "{{ service_required_packages }}"
  loop_control:
    label: "{{ item }}"

- name: Configure systemd service for each item in the service_list
  when: ansible_service_mgr == 'systemd'
  block:
    - name: Copy systemd service template
      template:
        src: systemd.j2
        dest: "/etc/systemd/system/{{ item.name }}.service"
        mode: '0644'
      loop: "{{ service_list }}"
      loop_control:
        label: "{{ item.name }}"

    - name: Reload systemd daemon
      systemd:
        daemon_reload: true
      notify: Systemctl daemon-reload

- name: Configure sysvinit service for each item in the service_list
  when: ansible_service_mgr in ['sysvinit', 'upstart', 'openrc']
  block:
    - name: Copy sysvinit service template
      template:
        src: sysvinit.j2
        dest: "/etc/init.d/{{ item.name }}"
        mode: '0755'
      loop: "{{ service_list }}"
      loop_control:
        label: "{{ item.name }}"

- name: Manage each service in the service_list
  service:
    name: "{{ item.name }}"
    state: "{{ item.state | default(omit) }}"
    enabled: "{{ item.enabled | default(omit) }}"
  loop: "{{ service_list }}"
  loop_control:
    label: "{{ item.name }}"

- name: Flush handlers
  meta: flush_handlers


